Why these six
-------------

nginx.conf includes go2rtc_upstream.conf, auth_location.conf, auth_request.conf
and proxy.conf directly; auth_location.conf in turn includes
proxy_trusted_headers.conf, so the sixth file is required for the configuration
to load at all.

Two more includes are named by nginx.conf and are absent here on purpose:

  listen.conf     generated in the container from templates/listen.gotmpl
  base_path.conf  generated in the container from templates/base_path.gotmpl

Neither exists in Frigate's source tree, so neither can be vendored. The
harness writes both, following those templates: listen.conf gets the two
`listen` lines the template emits with no TLS and no IPv6 section, at the
harness's own ports; base_path.conf is written empty, which is what the
template renders when no base path is configured.

Why the deployment's line numbers are these files' line numbers
--------------------------------------------------------------

The running pod's /usr/local/nginx/conf/nginx.conf was diffed against this
revision and differed on one line -- `worker_processes auto` against
`worker_processes 4` -- with no change in file length, and the four includes
matched the pod by md5. That measurement lives in
.agents/issue-2/RESEARCH-serving-contract.md; the md5 column above is the
source half of it, recomputed when these copies were taken.

mime.types is nginx's own, not Frigate's. The pod's copy maps
`application/wasm wasm;` at line 55 and so does the nginx this harness runs
(1.30.4), which is what makes the wasm content-type assertion meaningful here.
